==Finnish==

===Etymology===
A {{der|fi|gem}} loan, compare {{cog|gem-pro|*aldōn}} (whence eg. {{cog|no|olda}}). The ending has probably been modified to {{m|fi|-as}} by analogy with other Germanic loans (such as {{m|fi|valas}}). {{cog|krl|allaš||trough}} is of the same origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA}}
* {{hyphenation|al|las|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|ɑlːɑs}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[pool]], [[swimming pool]]
# [[tank]] {{gloss|open container for liquids}}
# [[basin]] {{gloss|wide bowl for washing}}
# {{lb|fi|geography}} [[basin]], [[drainage basin]] {{gloss|area of land from which water drains into a commom outlet}}
# [[reservoir]] {{gloss|natural or artificial lake used as a source of water supply}}
